972:
(a) Certificate of occupancy. A certificate of occupancy shall be required for any of the following:
(1) Occupancy and use of a building hereafter erected or enlarged;
(2) Change in use of an existing building to a different use;
(3) Occupancy and use of vacant land except for the raising of crops;
(4) Any change in a nonconforming use.
(b) After submitting plans and specifications to the building official and upon the issuance of a building permit, the builders will have complied with this chapter for all purposes, provided said building is constructed in accordance with said plans and specifications.
(c) No such occupancy, use, or charge of use shall take place until a certificate of occupancy therefore shall have been issued by the prescribed building official.
(d) A certificate of occupancy shall not be issued unless the proposed use of a building or land conforms to the applicable provisions of this chapter, or unless the building, as finally constructed, complies with the plans upon which the building permit was issued. The building official shall state in writing the reasons for denying such certificate of occupancy.
(Ord. of 8-11-1998, § 13-6)
